# What the image is NOT built from.
#
# MEASURED, not guessed: `docker build` streams the WHOLE directory to the daemon
# before it reads the first instruction. Here that was
#
#     Sending build context to Docker daemon  400.8MB
#
# of which `.git` is 260M and `docs/` is 110M — neither of which the image ever
# opens. Every build paid for both.
#
# THE RULE for editing this file: open the Dockerfile and read the `COPY` lines
# first. Everything they name must stay reachable; everything else is weight.
# What this image copies:
#     requirements.txt · wsgi.py · pyarchinit_mini/
#
# The templates, the static files and the compiled translations
# (`pyarchinit_mini/translations/*/LC_MESSAGES/*.mo`) are all INSIDE the package,
# so copying the package brings them. Measured, because the alternative — a
# static root at the repository root — would have made this file wrong: the app
# is `Flask(__name__)` with no `static_folder`/`template_folder` argument
# (`web_interface/app.py:536`), so both default to the package directory.
#
# This repository already knows most of its own weight: `.railwayignore` lists
# `.git`, `docs/`, `logo/`, `tests/`, `*.db`. That file is Railway's and only
# Railway reads it; this one is Docker's. The overlap is not duplication of a
# decision, it is two build systems each needing to be told.

# ── the big two ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
docs/

# ── the root logo, which nothing serves ──────────────────────────────────────
# MEASURED: `logo/logo_pyarchinit-mini.png` (1.0M) is referenced by no template,
# no stylesheet and no Python file. What the application actually serves is
# `app.static_folder/images/logo.png` (`web_interface/app.py:5159` and three
# more), i.e. `pyarchinit_mini/web_interface/static/images/logo.png`, which the
# package COPY brings in. Two files with one job, and only one of them is used.
logo/

# ── sample databases, and any other ──────────────────────────────────────────
# `data/` holds `pyarchinit_mini_sample.db` and `pyarchinit_tutorial.db` (316K).
# The container makes its own database at boot inside the volume; a sample one
# baked into the image would be a database somebody could mistake for theirs.
data/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ── virtual environments ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Host wheels compiled for macOS are useless inside Linux even if copied, and
# the image installs into its own environment from `requirements.txt`.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ── build and test leavings ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
node_modules/
output/

# ── the OTHER deliverables in this repository ────────────────────────────────
# This image is the Flask web interface. The Blender add-ons and the MCP server
# ship by their own routes and would only be weight here.
blender_addon/
blender_addons/

# ── tests, tooling and working notes ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The root is full of `test_*.py` scripts beside the `tests/` package; neither
# goes into a runtime image.
tests/
test_*.py
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.readthedocs.yaml
babel.cfg
MANIFEST.in
.claude/
# …and every Markdown file, README included. `stratigraph-server` copies its
# README because `pip install .` reads it through `pyproject.toml`; this image
# installs from `requirements.txt` and copies no README, so keeping one would be
# the rule I quoted above broken in the file that states it.
*.md

# ── deployment descriptors for OTHER targets ─────────────────────────────────
# Kept OUT deliberately, and it is worth saying why rather than leaving it to
# look like an oversight: this image mirrors `railway.toml`'s command (see the
# Dockerfile), but it does not need the file to do so — the command is written
# in the Dockerfile, where the image's own reader will look for it. Shipping
# both would put two start commands in one container again.
Procfile
railway.toml
.railwayignore
adarte_deploy.sh
.adarte_secrets.sh.example
.env.development

# ── the local database and secrets, if anyone ever runs the app in the tree ──
.pyarchinit_mini/
.DS_Store
